<title>SINGAPORE: Tuan Sing 1996 net up 140 pct.</title>
<headline>Tuan Sing 1996 net up 140 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    38.59  vs   16.09</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     0.50  vs    0.30</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    3.4   vs    1.42</p>
<p>    Turnover			     483.20  vs  293.86</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	4.90  vs    2.37</p>
<p>    Operating profit before tax     53.63  vs   28.69</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   7.41  vs    1.33</p>
<p>    Tax				    11.60   vs   11.66</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (loss)3.82    vs    1.66 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Tuan Sing Holdings Ltd is a diversified property group with interests and subsidiaries in electronics, construction, among other areas.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
